  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836346",
      "title": "Using Refs for More Than \"DOM Element Connections\"",
      "sourceHash": "4cd30b668d18c81746e5c8d65d97d4c957d8f2ba7029bb027558d13bd74fa8e8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 2.73,
          "en": "So how can we stop this timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.73,
          "end": 4.233,
          "en": "from inside this function?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.4,
          "end": 10.26,
          "en": "Well, JavaScript has a clear timeout function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.26,
          "end": 13.26,
          "en": "which can be used to stop a timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.26,
          "end": 16.11,
          "en": "but it needs a pointer at that timer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.11,
          "end": 19.923,
          "en": "the ID of that timer you could say as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.27,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "Now such a pointer is returned by setTimeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 30.453,
          "en": "So here we can store this timer in a constant, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 35.79,
          "en": "and therefore, of course, we could add a variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.79,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "timer outside of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 40.75,
          "en": "so that both functions can use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.06,
          "end": 45,
          "en": "and set it equal to the timer here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45,
          "end": 47.433,
          "en": "and then use it as a value in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.05,
          "end": 51.63,
          "en": "And now we just need to connect handleStop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.63,
          "end": 55.38,
          "en": "to this button if the timer is running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.38,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "And therefore we don't always want to pass handleStart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 63.603,
          "en": "to onClick but we want to check if timerStarted is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "And if that's the case, we wanna point at handleStop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 70.98,
          "en": "so that this function is executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "if this button is clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 77.163,
          "en": "and the timer was started and otherwise it's handleStart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "But now with that, handleStop should execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.633,
          "en": "if the timer is running and we should clear this timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 85.83,
          "end": 88.65,
          "en": "So if this works, we should not see you lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.65,
          "end": 92.223,
          "en": "after starting and stopping if we stop quick enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 95.943,
          "en": "So therefore, if I start this and stop this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 96.78,
          "end": 100.923,
          "en": "I still get you lost and I did press stop immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 101.75999999999999,
          "end": 105.753,
          "en": "So I start this, I stop this and still I get you lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 111.97999999999999,
          "en": "So somehow the timer was not stopped as it seems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 115.563,
          "en": "And the problem is that we're using a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 116.49000000000001,
          "end": 119.25,
          "en": "As you know, whenever state changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 119.25,
          "end": 122.94,
          "en": "this component function re-executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 122.94,
          "end": 124.8,
          "en": "And that, of course, also means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 124.8,
          "end": 127.263,
          "en": "that this variable is recreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 128.25,
          "end": 132.63,
          "en": "So the timer used in handleStop will be a different timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 132.63,
          "end": 135.36,
          "en": "than in handleStart because in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 135.36,
          "end": 137.7,
          "en": "the component function re-executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 137.7,
          "end": 140.523,
          "en": "because we updated the state in handleStart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "That's why we can't use this variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "Now, we could use this variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "if we define it outside of the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 152.043,
          "en": "because then it would not be recreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 153.12,
          "end": 157.07999999999998,
          "en": "And as a result, now if I reload this, if I start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 157.07999999999998,
          "end": 161.4,
          "en": "and stop, indeed we never see this you lost message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 161.4,
          "end": 163.8,
          "en": "Of course, this part here isn't updating.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 163.8,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "We'll take care about that later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 168.51,
          "en": "but we don't see the you lost message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 168.51,
          "end": 171.32999999999998,
          "en": "but we'll now face a different problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 171.32999999999998,
          "end": 174.15,
          "en": "And to show you which problem we'll face,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.15,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "I'll start the five second challenge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 179.82,
          "en": "Then immediately the one second challenge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 182.073,
          "en": "and then I'll stop both challenges.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183,
          "end": 186.9,
          "en": "So start five, start one, stop one, stop five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.9,
          "end": 189.42,
          "en": "And you'll see as a result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.42,
          "end": 193.2,
          "en": "I still get you lost here in the five second challenge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.2,
          "end": 194.583,
          "en": "even though I stopped it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.02,
          "end": 197.07,
          "en": "I'll show it to you again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 197.07,
          "end": 199.8,
          "en": "Start, start, stop, stop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.8,
          "end": 202.92000000000002,
          "en": "I did click here on the five second challenge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.92000000000002,
          "end": 207.92000000000002,
          "en": "Still, I get you lost and I don't get that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.99,
          "end": 211.263,
          "en": "if I just start and stop this challenge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 212.4,
          "end": 216.213,
          "en": "Now here I stopped it and therefore, I never get you lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 217.714,
          "end": 220.59,
          "en": "So why do I get this strange behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 220.59,
          "end": 222.93,
          "en": "where the five second challenge is lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 222.93,
          "end": 224.52,
          "en": "even though I stopped it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 224.52,
          "end": 227.913,
          "en": "if I also started and stopped the one second challenge?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.9,
          "end": 230.31,
          "en": "I'm getting that behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.31,
          "end": 234.45,
          "en": "because this timer variable is now a variable defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 234.45,
          "end": 237.27,
          "en": "in this TimerChallenge file outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 237.27,
          "end": 238.683,
          "en": "of this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 239.7,
          "end": 244.23,
          "en": "And therefore, it's actually a variable that will be shared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 244.23,
          "end": 248.4,
          "en": "across all component instances that are based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.4,
          "end": 249.993,
          "en": "on this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.07,
          "end": 255.09,
          "en": "And therefore, when I start the five seconds challenge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 255.09,
          "end": 257.28,
          "en": "this timer will store the timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257.28,
          "end": 258.94,
          "en": "of the five seconds challenge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.19,
          "end": 263.85,
          "en": "but if I then after starting the five seconds challenge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 263.85,
          "end": 266.34,
          "en": "also start the one second challenge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 266.34,
          "end": 270.18,
          "en": "timer here will be overwritten with a pointer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 270.18,
          "end": 272.253,
          "en": "at that one second timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 273.65999999999997,
          "end": 276.69,
          "en": "And that pointer at the five second timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 276.69,
          "end": 279.633,
          "en": "will basically be thrown away by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 280.71,
          "end": 283.74,
          "en": "Therefore, when I start this, start this, stop this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 283.74,
          "end": 284.76,
          "en": "and stop this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 284.76,
          "end": 288.54,
          "en": "I'm not stopping anything here in the five second challenge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 288.54,
          "end": 291.6,
          "en": "because that pointer at the five second timer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 291.6,
          "end": 296.04,
          "en": "was thrown away when I started the one second challenge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 296.04,
          "end": 299.67,
          "en": "because this variable here is defined in this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 299.67,
          "end": 302.58,
          "en": "and is therefore, shared across all instances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 302.58,
          "end": 303.723,
          "en": "of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 308.043,
          "en": "And that's why a variable is not the solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 308.97,
          "end": 311.19,
          "en": "So if a variable is not the solution,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 311.19,
          "end": 312.663,
          "en": "what is a solution then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.65,
          "end": 317.19,
          "en": "Well, refs can be a solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 317.19,
          "end": 320.34,
          "en": "because you cannot just use refs to connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 320.34,
          "end": 322.77,
          "en": "to HTML elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 322.77,
          "end": 325.92,
          "en": "even though that is a very common use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.92,
          "end": 330.92,
          "en": "but you can also use refs to manage any kind of value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 330.93,
          "end": 333.9,
          "en": "And therefore, here in this TimerChallenge component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 333.9,
          "end": 338.9,
          "en": "we can create a new ref, let's say a timer ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 340.62,
          "end": 343.203,
          "en": "a timer constant, which stores this ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 344.46,
          "end": 348.6,
          "en": "And we can now use this timer and set timer.current",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 348.6,
          "end": 351.93,
          "en": "because you always must target this current property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 351.93,
          "end": 354.933,
          "en": "as you learned and set this equal to the timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 356.64,
          "end": 359.28,
          "en": "And now we can clear the timeout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 359.28,
          "end": 361.72,
          "en": "by clearing it with timer.current",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 362.88,
          "end": 366.45,
          "en": "because in this current property, we'll store this pointer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 366.45,
          "end": 367.623,
          "en": "at this timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 368.82,
          "end": 371.49,
          "en": "And now since this is defined inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 371.49,
          "end": 372.81,
          "en": "of the component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 372.81,
          "end": 375.993,
          "en": "it will be component instance specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 377.25,
          "end": 379.14,
          "en": "Every component instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 379.14,
          "end": 381.24,
          "en": "of this TimerChallenge component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 381.24,
          "end": 385.53,
          "en": "will get its own timer ref that works totally independent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 387.57,
          "en": "from the other refs that belong",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 387.57,
          "end": 390.093,
          "en": "to the other instances of that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 391.26,
          "end": 394.77,
          "en": "But at the same time, unlike variables defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 394.77,
          "end": 398.7,
          "en": "in component functions, this ref will not be reset",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 398.7,
          "end": 401.88,
          "en": "or cleared when this component re-executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 401.88,
          "end": 404.82,
          "en": "Instead, just as with state values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 404.82,
          "end": 407.82,
          "en": "React will store these timer values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 407.82,
          "end": 410.25,
          "en": "behind the scenes and make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 410.25,
          "end": 412.26,
          "en": "that they don't get lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 412.26,
          "end": 415.65,
          "en": "as this component function re-executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 415.65,
          "end": 419.04,
          "en": "That's another special thing about refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 419.04,
          "end": 422.7,
          "en": "Like state values, the value here is not lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 422.7,
          "end": 425.43,
          "en": "when this component function re-executes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 425.43,
          "end": 428.43,
          "en": "But unlike state, setting this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 428.43,
          "end": 432.25,
          "en": "also doesn't cause this component function to execute again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 433.68,
          "end": 438.42,
          "en": "and therefore, now with that, finally, we can save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 438.42,
          "end": 442.173,
          "en": "and start and stop this and we don't get you lost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 443.64,
          "end": 445.26,
          "en": "And I can now also start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 445.26,
          "end": 447.99,
          "en": "and stop both challenges and stop both",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 447.99,
          "end": 450.933,
          "en": "and I never get you lost in any of the two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 452.15999999999997,
